EXPLAIN FORMAT=TREE
SELECT alias2.col_int_key, alias1.col_int_nokey, alias2.col_varchar_key
FROM ptrc_sem_cc AS alias1, ptrc_sem_cc AS alias2
WHERE NOT(alias2.col_int_key >= ANY
(SELECT /*+ PRC_SUBQUERY() */ sq2.col_int_nokey
FROM ptrc_sem_cc AS sq1, ptrc_sem_c AS sq2
WHERE sq1.col_int_key = alias1.col_int_key
GROUP BY 1));
EXPLAIN
-> Nested loop inner join  (...)
    -> Index scan on alias1 using col_int_key_3  (...)
    -> Result cache : cache keys(alias1.col_int_key, alias1.col_int_nokey)  (...)
        -> Filter: <not>(<in_optimizer>(alias2.col_int_key,<exists>(select #2)))  (...)
            -> Index scan on alias2 using col_int_key_2  (...)
            -> Select #2 (subquery in condition; dependent)
                -> Result cache : cache keys(alias1.col_int_key, alias2.col_int_key)
                    -> Limit: 1 row(s)  (...)
                        -> Nested loop inner join  (...)
                            -> Filter: <if>(outer_field_is_not_null, (<cache>(alias2.col_int_key) >= sq2.col_int_nokey), true)  (...)
                                -> Table scan on sq2  (...)
                            -> Result cache : cache keys(alias1.col_int_key, alias2.col_int_key, sq2.col_int_nokey)  (...)
                                -> Covering index lookup on sq1 using col_int_key (col_int_key=alias1.col_int_key)  (...)

Warnings:
Note	1276	Field or reference 'test.alias1.col_int_key' of SELECT #2 was resolved in SELECT #1
